title: Banking Crisis
subtitle: The imminent collapse of the German banking system...
new-page: true
on-arrival: banking_crisis_seen = 1
tags: event
view-if: year = 1931 and month = 7
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/danat_bank.jpg

= Banking Crisis

The Darmstädter und Nationalbank, or Danat Bank, is on the verge of collapse! Along with it would go much of the German banking system. The cause seemed to be due to the government's pursuit of a [? if austria_annexed == 0: customs ?] union with Austria, which led to de facto international sanctions.

- @banking_crisis_avoided: The banking system manages to remain solvent!
- @banking_crisis_hit: The banks fail.

@banking_crisis_avoided
subtitle: Thanks to our previous creation of deposit insurance, the banks limp forward.
choose-if: deposit_insurance
unavailable-subtitle: We have not establish a deposit insurance.
on-arrival: workers_dvp += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_dvp += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_dvp += 8*(1-dissent); rural_dvp += 4*(1-dissent); liberal_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 10; industrialist_dissent -= 10; nationalist_dissent -= 5; economic_growth += 1.2;

Our wise choice to create a bank bailout with our control of the Reichsbank has proven to borne fruit, the impending crisis never hits and we see our support increase across all demographics.

@banking_crisis_hit
view-if: deposit_insurance == 0
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 5; workers_nsdap += 3; new_middle_nsdap += 3; old_middle_nsdap += 4; rural_nsdap += 3; unemployed += 3; crisis_urgency += 1; workers_dvp -= 4 if dvp_in_government; new_middle_dvp -= 5 if dvp_in_government; old_middle_dvp -= 5 if dvp_in_government; rural_dvp -= 4 if dvp_in_government; economic_growth -= 1;

Unemployement ticks up once more and the extremist parties see increased support.

- @enact_austerity: We shall cut welfare.
- @stabilization: Take action to stabilize the economy!
- @spd_stabilization: The social democrats take emergency action to stabilize the economy.
- @austerity: Chancellor [+ chancellor +]'s response is, as always, more austerity.
- @end_toleration: We are tired of austerity. End the toleration arrangement!

@enact_austerity
view-if: dvp_in_government
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; spd_relation -= 5; new_middle_dvp -= 3; old_middle_dvp -= 3; pro_republic -= 3

Our expected course of action, though it doesn't earn us any supporters or goodwill.

@stabilization
view-if: dvp_in_government
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: workers_dvp += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); rural_dvp += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 2; inflation += 1 if inflation < 0; budget -= 1; workers_nsdap -= 3; economic_growth += 0.9;

In the face of the banking crisis, we have taken emergency action to stabilize the economy by injecting money into the banking system. It might not be enough, but it temporarily staunches the bleeding.

@spd_stabilization
view-if: spd_in_government and dvp_in_government == 0
on-arrival: workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 2; inflation += 1 if inflation < 0; budget -= 1; workers_nsdap -= 3; economic_growth += 1;

The <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> moves quickly to stabilize the economy by injecting money into the banking system. It might not be enough, but it temporarily staunches the bleeding.

@austerity
view-if: spd_in_government == 0 and dvp_in_government == 0
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; pro_republic -= 3; economic_growth -= 1;

Chancellor [+ chancellor +] responds to the banking crisis with more cuts to welfare.

@end_toleration
view-if: dvp_toleration = 1
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; in_grand_coalition = 0; dvp_toleration = 0;
call: set_next_election_time

We are tired of [+ chancellor +]'s policy of austerity. After [+ chancellor +]'s attempt to use emergency powers to pass another welfare cut, we have worked with the other parties to reverse this policy. In response, the Reichstag has been dissolved, and new elections called.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
